<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banten</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Banten is a province at the western tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, separated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-java">West Java</a> in 2000. Its old port of Banten, on the bay of the same name, was the centre of the Banten Sultanate, founded after Muslim forces from Demak and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a> took it from the Sunda Kingdom in the 1520s, and became one of Asia's great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a> ports. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> gained control of it in the late 17th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banten.jpg" alt="Banten" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banten_in_Indonesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
